# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 51. a rival's result contradicts yours (triads D2b)
# Round 5, 2026-10-07 (P10): per_year back to the times line (calibration had cut it to .01 .01 .003).

== a rival's result contradicts yours
tier: life event
stages: adult mature elder
age: 28-95
holds: published research
per_year: 0 0 0 .03 .03 .01
drivers: era+.2 trouble+.1
times: per person with published research a year: about 3 in 100 adults and people in midlife and 1 in 100 elders see a rival group publish a result that contradicts one of theirs; large replication projects in several fields have repeated only about half of the published findings they tried, so most people who publish for many years meet such a challenge (estimate)
likelier: a well-known finding, a crowded field, small samples in the original work, a rival group on the same question
rarer: a quiet corner of a field, findings already repeated many times, work nobody else can afford to repeat
domain: career.5
tone: trouble
life: work, meaning
horizon: months
roles: rival, colleague, mentor
earth: a rival group publishes a result that says your best-known finding is wrong
scene: The new issue of the journal has a paper from {rival}'s group, and its title says, in effect, that {Ns} best-known finding does not hold. Colleagues have already started forwarding it, with question marks.
scene W: There is a proper way to settle this: the evidence laid out in the open and judged by people with no stake in either side. {N} believes in that way, even now.
scene U: {N} reads the methods section twice, slowly. Somewhere in it is the difference between the two studies, and finding it matters more than winning.
scene B: {rival} has wanted this for years. {N} feels the challenge like a shove in a crowd, and has no intention of stepping aside.
scene R: {Ns} pulse is up before the abstract is finished. It feels personal, and part of {N} wants to pick up the phone right now.
scene G: Findings are like trees: some stand for a century, some fall in the first storm. {N} has seen both, and waits to see which this one is.
- W | ask an independent lab to repeat both studies, and accept what it finds | grants: a finding that held up | v: universalism, conformity | chance: 50
- U | repeat your own experiment step by step, with their method alongside | grants: a finding that held up | v: achievement, universalism | chance: 60
